Minimal fix: in src/app.html bayThrow (line 796), skip the chart for a straight-up throw. The verdict, Height tile and drag bullet already give the height, time and drag loss.

  if (!f.relativistic && f.path && f.path.length > 1 && !straightUp) {

Optional extra guard: also put a floor on the x-axis in trajectoryChart (line 596), so no future case can scale an axis to round-off:

  maxX = Math.max(maxX, maxY / 20) || 1; maxY = maxY || 1;

With that floor, a vertical flight would draw as a vertical line at x = 0, not a femtometre-wide parabola. A height-vs-time plot would need fly() to record t on each path point. Path points currently hold only [x, h, keepFlag], so that is a larger change than this fix needs.

In src/app.html bayJump, after rFree is computed, add:
  const groundLimits = r.heldBack && rFree && (rFree.flight.escaped || rFree.flight.apex > f.apex * 1.02);

Chip: change `else if (r.heldBack) gchip = status('warn', 'Ground at its limit: he holds back');` to
  else if (groundLimits) gchip = status('warn', 'Ground at its limit: he holds back');
  else if (r.heldBack) gchip = status('good', 'Ground holds: he keeps under its limit');
Use this explicit label. Do not fall through to the existing else branch: r.F is the dial force, so that branch would say "his feet barely dent it", which is wrong here because there is no dent.

Bullet: keep the current sentence only when groundLimits is true. Otherwise (r.heldBack && !groundLimits) push:
  'On ' + c.surface.short + ' his feet can push off with at most ' + fmtSI(RB, 'N') + ' before it gives, so he keeps his push under that; pushing harder would only sink his feet. It costs him nothing: rigid ground gives the same height, because ' + (state.mode === 'real' ? 'real muscle’s leg speed' : 'his legs') + ', not the ground, sets the height.'

