The tile and bullet need no change. Rebuild dist and rerun test/calibration.js.

In throwOnce (src/engine.js, around line 699), evaluate the sink check at the stroke's mean push in real mode instead of the isometric peak. Leave comic mode, which uses a constant force, unchanged:

    // Real muscle: the isometric peak lasts only an instant (it hands the object its momentum almost at once);
    // load the ground with the push the stroke actually averaged.
    const Fsink = ctx.mode === 'real' && push.xA + push.xB > 0 ? push.work / (push.xA + push.xB) : Fused;
    const Nfeet = isFinite(Fsink) ? anc.N(Fsink) : (Math.sin(th) > 1e-12 ? Infinity : anc.N(0));

This alone fixes both the finite cases and the ∞ case. Do not use the `>=` tie-break as the fix: it leaves ∞ broken and sets heldBack = true on ties, which shows a false "waste the throw" bullet. If you also want ties settled consistently, add something like `else if (held.pB >= push.pB * (1 - 1e-9) && Fc < Fused) Fused = Fc;` without touching heldBack. Separately, consider letting the cap loop run in real mode when F is ∞ (pushApartHill already clamps F0), so a real-mode throw at ∞ is no longer slower than at 1e9 kg.

Only src/app.html bayJump needs to change. rFree is already computed whenever heldBack is true. After `const RB = ...; const rFree = ...;` add:

  const groundBinds = r.heldBack && rFree && (rFree.flight.escaped || rFree.flight.apex > 1.01 * f.apex);

